description = "M28AI companion, campaign only. Enables M28AI's combined AI/human armies (per-unit, manual takeover of your own units) in single-player campaigns, where the game rebuilds ScenarioInfo.Options and drops all lobby game options. Also enforces AI-inherit at the engine event level so units built by a taken-over factory/engineer really do inherit the takeover (M28AI's own propagation is unreliable on the retail build). Units are never taken over until you toggle them. v9 fixes a takeover that switched itself off when a factory finished building: player intent now comes only from the toggle click, never inferred from unit state, and a missing M28CombinedArmy option is restored automatically if the campaign rebuilds its Options table. v10 adds experimental fire spreading: a group of taken-over experimentals no longer all shells the same enemy, extra units shift to nearby less-contested targets (ACU/SACU/enemy experimentals/T3 structures stay exempt so priority kills get full weight), and a locked target now holds for 8 seconds (12 for experimentals) unless a high-value target appears. v11 cuts reconcile load: only your own units are tracked (enemy AI units were being tracked and their UI stats rewritten for nothing, thousands of C calls a second), the built/completed check is cached per unit, and the reconcile thread now stops immediately when the last tracked unit disappears instead of idling for 20 more seconds into the end-of-mission cleanup. v12 hardens the sweep against the end-of-mission teardown that crashed two sessions: it stands down for 20 seconds when more than half of your tracked units vanish inside one pass, never calls GetStat/UpdateStat on a unit whose Dead flag is set, and re-checks each unit once its brain attaches so enemy units no longer pad the registry. It also fixes a target pin that never expired (the timer was renewed even on the passes where the wrapper had just overridden the choice, so a unit could stay locked on one enemy forever), and wraps the three behaviour hooks in pcall so an error can never kill M28AI's command thread. v8's aggression tuning is still in: lower enemy-threat valuation, no dodge/hover micro, original fast order cycle, no retreat micro for your land combat units, and a reroll when a factory would repeat its last pick. M28AI keeps full control of its own housekeeping, including destroying surplus units; no unit or factory caps are applied, and M28AI itself is never modified. Requires M28AI v328 enabled; harmless no-op otherwise. Skirmish and multiplayer behaviour is never touched."
